  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41123-PROJECT-210284</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41123" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations Industrial Development Organization</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kigali HFC implementation plan (stage I)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project seeks to implement stage I of the Kigali HFC Implementation Plan (KIP) to help Rwanda achieve a 10% reduction in its HFC baseline consumption by January 1, 2029. The total cost of stage I is US $192 ,100, which includes US $100,000 for UNEP (plus US $13,000 in agency support costs) and US $70,000 for UNIDO (plus US $9,100 in agency support costs). The first tranche of stage I, amounting to US $77 ,970, covers activities from January 2025 to December 2027. It includes US $44,000 for UNEP (plus US $5,720 in support costs) and US $25,000 for UNIDO (plus US $3,250 in support costs). The project will focus on regulatory and policy measures, capacity building, and technical assistance to help Rwanda transition to low-GWP alternatives, aligning with the targets set under the Kigali Amendment.</narrative>
  </description>
